\ The sample code the Board tab gives for SPI flash, as generated  ok.
\ (SamplesTest checks that it still matches): a W25Q64 on SPI1, a W25Q32 on SPI2.  ok.
#!attach 1 flash PA4 PA5 PA7 PA6
#!attach 2 flash PB12 PB13 PB15 PB14 size=32
  ok.
\ flash: W25Q64 flash, 8 MB, on SPI1: CS PA4, CLK PA5, DI PA7, DO PA6  ok.
\ Paste all of it into the console, or put it in a file after wiring.fs.  ok.
  ok.
\ PA4 (pin 18) → W25Q64 CS; WP and HOLD → 3V3, VCC → 3V3, GND → GND, 100 nF from VCC to GND  ok.
$48000000 constant flash-cs-port  \ GPIOA  ok.
4 constant flash-cs-pin  ok.
\ PA5 (pin 19) → W25Q64 CLK  ok.
$48000000 constant flash-clk-port  \ GPIOA  ok.
5 constant flash-clk-pin  ok.
$40013000 constant flash-spi  \ SPI1  ok.
5 constant flash-clk-af  ok.
\ PA7 (pin 21) → W25Q64 DI (data into the flash)  ok.
$48000000 constant flash-di-port  \ GPIOA  ok.
7 constant flash-di-pin  ok.
5 constant flash-di-af  ok.
\ PA6 (pin 20) ← W25Q64 DO (data out of the flash)  ok.
$48000000 constant flash-do-port  \ GPIOA  ok.
6 constant flash-do-pin  ok.
5 constant flash-do-af  ok.
  ok.
\ ms: wait n milliseconds, counted by SysTick at 16 MHz  ok.
\ (lib_systick uses SysTick too: with it loaded, use its delay-ms)  ok.
: ms ( n -- )  ok.
  15999 $E000E014 !  0 $E000E018 !  5 $E000E010 ! \ SysTick: wrap every 16000 cycles  ok.
  0 ?do begin $E000E010 @ $10000 and until loop   \ count the wraps  ok.
  0 $E000E010 ! ;                                 \ SysTick off again  ok.
  ok.
: flash-sr ( -- u ) flash-spi 8 + @ ;             \ SPI1 SR  ok.
: >flash> ( b -- b )                              \ one byte out, one byte in  ok.
  begin flash-sr 2 and until  flash-spi $C + c!   \ wait for TXE; c! writes one frame  ok.
  begin flash-sr 1 and until  flash-spi $C + c@ ; \ wait for RXNE: the byte that came back  ok.
: flash-on ( c -- )                               \ CS low, then the command byte  ok.
  1 flash-cs-pin lshift 16 lshift flash-cs-port $18 + !  >flash> drop ;  ok.
: flash-off ( -- ) 1 flash-cs-pin lshift flash-cs-port $18 + ! ; \ CS high: the command ends here  ok.
: >flash-addr ( a -- )                            \ 24-bit address, high byte first  ok.
  dup 16 rshift >flash> drop  dup 8 rshift >flash> drop  >flash> drop ;  ok.
: flash-status ( -- u ) 5 flash-on 0 >flash> flash-off ; \ status register 1: BUSY bit 0, WEL bit 1  ok.
: flash-wait ( -- ) begin flash-status 1 and 0= until ; \ until a program or erase is done  ok.
: flash-wren ( -- ) 6 flash-on flash-off ;        \ write enable, before every program and erase  ok.
: flash-id ( -- )                                 \ JEDEC ID: EF Winbond, 40, then the size  ok.
  $9F flash-on  0 >flash> hex. 0 >flash> hex. 0 >flash> hex.  flash-off ;  ok.
: flash-read ( a addr u -- )                      \ u bytes from the flash at a to memory at addr  ok.
  rot 3 flash-on >flash-addr  ok.
  0 ?do 0 >flash> over i + c! loop drop flash-off ;  ok.
: flash-write ( addr u a -- )                     \ u bytes to the flash at a, within one 256-byte page  ok.
  flash-wren 2 flash-on >flash-addr  ok.
  0 ?do dup i + c@ >flash> drop loop drop flash-off flash-wait ; \ it programs when CS goes high  ok.
: flash-erase ( a -- )                            \ the 4 KB sector around a, back to FF  ok.
  flash-wren $20 flash-on >flash-addr flash-off flash-wait ; \ takes about 45 ms  ok.
  ok.
: flash-init ( -- )  ok.
  1 0 lshift $4002104C bis!                       \ RCC AHB2ENR: clock for GPIOA  ok.
  1 12 lshift $40021060 bis!                      \ RCC APB2ENR: clock for SPI1  ok.
  flash-off                                       \ CS high before it becomes an output  ok.
  %11 flash-cs-pin 2* lshift flash-cs-port bic!   \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %01 flash-cs-pin 2* lshift flash-cs-port bis!   \ MODER: 01 = output  ok.
  1 flash-cs-pin lshift flash-cs-port 4 + bic!    \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  %11 flash-clk-pin 2* lshift flash-clk-port bic! \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %10 flash-clk-pin 2* lshift flash-clk-port bis! \ MODER: 10 = alternate function  ok.
  1 flash-clk-pin lshift flash-clk-port 4 + bic!  \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  $F flash-clk-pin 4 * lshift flash-clk-port $20 + bic! \ AFRL: clear the four bits  ok.
  flash-clk-af flash-clk-pin 4 * lshift flash-clk-port $20 + bis! \ AFRL: AF5 = SPI1 SCK  ok.
  %11 flash-di-pin 2* lshift flash-di-port bic!   \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %10 flash-di-pin 2* lshift flash-di-port bis!   \ MODER: 10 = alternate function  ok.
  1 flash-di-pin lshift flash-di-port 4 + bic!    \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  $F flash-di-pin 4 * lshift flash-di-port $20 + bic! \ AFRL: clear the four bits  ok.
  flash-di-af flash-di-pin 4 * lshift flash-di-port $20 + bis! \ AFRL: AF5 = SPI1 MOSI  ok.
  %11 flash-do-pin 2* lshift flash-do-port bic!   \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %10 flash-do-pin 2* lshift flash-do-port bis!   \ MODER: 10 = alternate function  ok.
  1 flash-do-pin lshift flash-do-port 4 + bic!    \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  $F flash-do-pin 4 * lshift flash-do-port $20 + bic! \ AFRL: clear the four bits  ok.
  flash-do-af flash-do-pin 4 * lshift flash-do-port $20 + bis! \ AFRL: AF5 = SPI1 MISO  ok.
  $1700 flash-spi 4 + !                           \ CR2: 8-bit frames, RXNE after one byte (FRXTH)  ok.
  $354 flash-spi ! ;                              \ CR1: master, SCK = 16 MHz / 8, SSM and SSI (CS is a GPIO), on  ok.
  ok.
\ Erase a sector, write a line, read it back  ok.
: flash-hello s" Hello from Forth" ;  ok.
64 buffer: flash-buf  ok.
: flash-demo ( -- )  ok.
  flash-init flash-id cr  ok.
  0 flash-erase  flash-hello 0 flash-write  ok.
  0 flash-buf 16 flash-read  flash-buf 16 type ;  ok.
  ok.
\ Try it: flash-init flash-id   or   flash-demo  ok.
